  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 345 AM EDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\n- Waiting on the storms today\n\nAs suspected, the convection in this northwest flow regime has \nvastly underperformed so far for Lower Michigan despite the hi \nres convective models insisting on bringing it in. So we wait to\nsee when and if we get anything. Latest trends show an uptick in \nthe storms across northern Minnesota, but that's a long way off\nand the rain across Wisconsin is decreasing as it crosses Lake\nMichigan so we will continue to wait. If the storms do finally \nget here, hail and downburst winds will be the main threats.\n\nWhatever convection does reach us today should be pushing south \nthis evening with some lingering showers possible after midnight \nas a surface low and trailing front clears the forecast area. \nSurface high builds in with fair weather for Tuesday and \nWednesday.\n\n- Next chance for rain end of the week\n\nAn upper level shortwave trough rounds the top of the western\nCONUS ridge and cuts off across the Great Lakes on Friday and\nSaturday with showers and thunderstorms possible for those two\ndays.",
